d 'WRITEINPUT': module to turn the data in memory into a self-contained, reproducible input command block
d
d  writeinput converts the data in memory, or a filtered subset of
d it, into an input command a reader can paste to reconstruct the
d dataset exactly - the standard way to post a minimum working
d example on Statalist or Stack Overflow. It is built for
d bit-for-bit fidelity: precision(hex) writes doubles as %21x so
d nothing is lost in the round trip, extended missing values (.a
d through .z) are detected and preserved, and every string is
d wrapped in compound double quotes so internal quotes and
d backticks cannot break the block. Works with frames, if/in, and
d random sample drawing; variable labels can be emitted as comments
d and value labels decoded into the example. Output goes to a .do
d file, to the results window (dryrun), or as a fenced code block
d for GitHub (markdown). 
d
d KW: reproducible example; data management; Statalist; input
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f writeinput.ado
f writeinput.sthlp
